===Pokémon Adventures===
====History====
====={{MangaArc|Gold, Silver & Crystal}}=====
In ''[[PS153|Oh, It's Ho-Oh!]]'', a male and female Poké Fan go towards the [[Indigo Plateau]] with their {{p|Pikachu}}.

In ''[[PS159|The Last Battle XIII]]'', a male and female Poké Fan appeared as two of the Trainers that lent their Pokémon for the final battle against the [[Masked Man]].

====={{MangaArc|Emerald}}=====
In ''[[PS308|As Luck Would Have It, Kirlia]]'' and ''[[PS309|Moving Past Milotic]]'', {{adv|Emerald}} has a [[Double Battle]] at the [[Battle Pike]], against virtual male and female Poké Fans who use {{p|Kirlia}} and {{p|Dusclops}}.

====={{MangaArc|HeartGold & SoulSilver}}=====
In ''[[PS446|Weavile Wobbles But It Won't Fall Down]]'', a female Poké Fan and her son appeared amongst the people at the [[Safari Zone Gate]].

====={{MangaArc|Platinum}}=====
In ''[[PS418|Deprogramming Porygon-Z]]'', a female Poké Fan was seen entering the [[Battle Castle]] with her {{p|Bonsly}}.

====={{MangaArc|Black & White}}=====
A male and a female Poké Fan appeared in ''[[PS466|An Odd Speech]]'', listening to [[Ghetsis]]' speech.

====={{MangaArc|X & Y}}=====
In ''[[PS554|Kangaskhan...Kangascan't]]'', a male Poké Fan appeared at [[Santalune City]] with his son and their {{p|Inkay}}. Another male Poké Fan without a son walks past {{adv|Shauna}} after she ran off from the others for easily trusting [[Viola]].

A female Poké Fan with her son was seen in {{adv|Blue}}'s flashback in ''[[PS582|Pinsir Glares]]''.

In ''[[PS593|Xerneas Gives]]'', a female Poké Fan with her daughter appeared at Lumiose City.

