==Trivia==
* In all of the games, the species of the dolls accompanying the female Poké Fan sprite shown changes (progressing with {{p|Clefairy}}, {{p|Wailmer}}, {{p|Bonsly}}, {{p|Sewaddle}}, {{p|Flabébé}}, {{p|Banette}}, {{p|Skitty}}, and {{p|Pancham}}), but until [[Pokémon X and Y]], the male Poké Fan sprite has always been shown holding a child in a {{p|Pikachu}} or {{p|Pichu}} costume, as well as the Pokémon's icon imprinted onto their T-shirts.
* Because the female Poké Fan sprite remains the same between Diamond, Pearl, and Platinum and HeartGold and SoulSilver, they are shown to have {{p|Bonsly}} dolls in [[Johto|a region]] where Sudowoodo appears only once (and is apparently not well-known) and where Bonsly does not appear in [[List of Pokémon by Johto Pokédex number|the regional Pokédex]].
* The Poké Fan is voiced by Kaiji Tang in [[Pokémon Masters EX]].

